  "id": "lorenz-attractor-phy",
  "name": "Lorenz Attractor",
  "description": "A simplified mathematical model for atmospheric convection that exhibits chaotic behavior. The system's extreme sensitivity to initial conditions gave rise to the concept of the 'butterfly effect'. With standard parameters, solutions trace out the famous butterfly-shaped strange attractor. Reference: Lorenz, E. N. (1963). Deterministic nonperiodic flow. Journal of the Atmospheric Sciences, 20(2), 130-141. DOI: https://doi.org/10.1175/1520-0469(1963)020<0130:DNF>2.0.CO;2",
